{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":984524,"ns":0,"title":"Apophenia","extract":"Apophenia () is the tendency to perceive meaningful connections between unrelated things. The term (German: Apophänie from the Greek verb: ἀποφαίνειν, romanized: apophaínein) was coined by psychiatrist Klaus Conrad in his 1958 publication on the beginning stages of schizophrenia.","description":"Tendency to perceive connections between unrelated things","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}